Good afternoon,

From what I can see, the landlord has promised a vacant unit for your use d=
uring the time of the renovation. They also said the renovations should tak=
e approximately 2 =E2=80=93 3 weeks.

For the list of renovation items, please speak directly to the landlord, as=
 I can not make promises on their behalf. As RTB/lg has stated below, you h=
ave a right to refuse the renovations if you are deeming them to be unneces=
sary. The down side to this, is that if the landlord has extensive renovati=
ons to complete, they can terminate the tenancy.

I do not believe that this is something that the RTB needs to determine wit=
h the landlord, but more so something that you need to decide on. The decis=
ion is whether or not you will allow the landlord to perform the renovation=
s as they have requested, or whether you will refuse them. Each option has =
pros and cons. You will need to decide wht works best for your situation.

Thank you

Leighsha Napoletano
