The right of first refusal refers to a tenants right to move back in once t=
he renovations are complete. It does not imply any right to refuse the reno=
vations.
If you refuse to move out based on the notice the landlord has the right to=
 file for an Order of Possession.
Assuming that the landlord had followed the procedure correctly (using prop=
er form, following proper timeline) it could be a very easy win for them if=
 they pursued an eviction against you, in such a situation.
If the landlord does not do the renovations within six months of the tenant=
 moving out, the tenant can come back and make a claim against the landlord=
 on the basis that they gave the notice in bad faith. This can include clai=
ming for the difference of your rent for up to twelve months.
The landlord has no obligation to provide you with an alternative apartment=
 while they are doing the renovations.
The landlord must provide a breakdown of the renovations they intend to do =
and an estimate of what the rent will be when the renovations are complete.

RTB/SS

